INV-bigaz / INV-dohoj. smart-test unions the tests that read a changed
catalogue YAML, and the union was right. Its KEY was not: a regex naming
io_primitives and io_primitives_overlays, which is 23 of the 169 YAML
files the wheel ships.

Measured on dev 81f1a69f88, a change confined to frameworks/ (107 files),
dataflow_patterns/, cfg_nodes/, function_summaries/ or taint_sources/
selected ZERO tests, wrote a 0-test manifest, printed "no test-relevant
files changed (docs/config only)" -- asserting the opposite of what had
happened -- and ci.yml then skipped pytest. A fix keyed to one instance
left the class and looked done.

The key is now the SHAPE of shipped data, and the grep terms are derived
per family from hypergumbo_core.yaml_catalogs.YAML_CATALOGS -- the
registry validate_registry() already gates against the tree, so the
eleventh family arrives covered by the commit that registers it. Three
arms: the directory name, the loader module the registry names, and the
load_* entry points read out of that loader's source. The loader arm is
load-bearing and that is measured: the directory name alone reaches 58
test files, the union reaches 157.

Families sharing a loader reach each other, which is what keeps the
widening from NARROWING -- the old key fired one shared rule for both
io_primitives directories, and the literal io_primitives does not appear
in every test that reads them.

The helper parses the registry with ast rather than importing it, so
selection never depends on the package being installed, and a registry
that cannot be read degrades to the changed directory's own name rather
than to silence.

